NAME
     sfdisk - partition a disk

SYNOPSIS
     sfdisk [-l] [--label dos|gpt] DEVICE
     fdisk -l DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
     sfdisk prints a partition table with -l, and writes one from the
     lines it reads on standard input otherwise: start, size and type
     per partition. Both the DOS and the GPT layouts are understood.

OPTIONS
     -l              print the table
     --label TYPE    which kind of table to write

SEE ALSO
     blockdev(8), losetup(8), mkfs_ext4(8)
